cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "streamdiar: online bounded-latency speaker diarization with a measured DER/latency tradeoff"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch online speaker diarizer that commits a speaker label for every
  window within a fixed emission delay, with the offline global-clustering
  reference implemented in the same codebase as the infinite-latency asymptote.
  The deliverable is the measured DER-versus-latency curve, with every difference
  placed against the run-to-run noise scale sqrt(2)*sd from a three-seed study.
  Causality is a structural guarantee, asserted bit-identically under future
  perturbation rather than argued.
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmad
    given-names: Arslan
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/arslan-ahmad/streaming-speaker-diarization"
keywords:
